    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Syst??????me de cote ??????nerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="11" build="21119">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.11b21119</English>
                <French>v15.11b21119</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="21119">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b21119</English>
                <French>v1.16b21119</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="1" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="1" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Receptacles

- All windows

- All doors

- Bathroom fan

- Furnace chimney

- Foundation wall and header joist



During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings and comfort.

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, the attic insulation inspection was not possible. We estimated the insulation level according to be R-19. We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. </ceilings>
                <foundation>At the time of the assessment, the basement insulation was R-12, we recommend to increase the insulation level. Also, we recommend to add more insulation on the header joist, we notice a high air leakage from this area during the infiltration test. </foundation>
                <windows>All windows leaks and therefore represent a large portion of the air leakage. We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple-pane and Energy-star certified units. </windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="" />
        </Options>
